  <diagram id="05-assurance-level-matrix" name="05-assurance-level-matrix" description="A grid of sixteen cells, with impact of error up the side from 1 at the bottom to 4 at the top, and likelihood of error along the bottom from 1 low to 4 very high. Impact 4 is Level 4 BCA at every likelihood, and that row is outlined. Impact 3 is Level 1 Standard at likelihood 1, Level 2 Enhanced at 2, and Level 3 Comprehensive at 3 and 4. Impact 2 is Level 1 Standard at likelihood 1, Level 2 Enhanced at 2 and 3, and Level 3 Comprehensive at 4. Impact 1 is Level 1 Standard at likelihood 1 to 3, and Level 2 Enhanced at 4. Beside the grid, two notes: any impact dimension scored 4 gives Level 4 BCA, whatever the likelihood; and complexity is one likelihood dimension, which does not set the level on its own.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="680" pageHeight="500" math="0" shadow="0" background="#F0F4F5">
